---
<!doctype html><html lang="en-CA"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><title>Our standards | PictureThis Production</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"/></head><body><a href="#main">Skip to content</a><SiteHeader/><main id="main"><PageHero eyebrow="Policies" title="Our standards" id="34598087" alt="Professional camera operator in a production venue"/><section class="page-opening"><p>These lines are public promises. The full policies sit behind them (policies-draft.md) and are available to funders, partners and families on request.</p></section><section><ul><li>Every mentor passes a Vulnerable Sector Check before working with participants and follows a written code of conduct.</li><li>Mentors and participants meet in crew spaces, never alone off-site.</li><li>Participants aged 16 and 17 join with a parent or guardian's consent, and a parent or guardian can reach the program lead at any time.</li><li>Photos and recordings of participants are used only with consent, and consent can be withdrawn.</li><li>The program is free, and it stays free. No fees, no gear purchases, no paid upsells.</li><li>Anyone can raise a concern, about safety, conduct or anything else, and it will be heard by a named person, not a form. (Contact route to be confirmed by Rey.)</li></ul></section></main><SiteFooter/></body></html>